msgstr "使用同一个不常见的客户端：窗口内至多 3 个账户使用过的 User-Agent，且各自至少发送了 2 个请求"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:30
msgid ""
"An address is an IPv4 address or an IPv6 /64, because a host's temporary "
"IPv6 addresses change inside its /64. Registrations are self-service "
"sign-ups by email, phone or single sign-on; an account an administrator "
"created is not one. Sign-ins are successful ones only."
msgstr ""
"这里的地址指一个 IPv4 地址或一个 IPv6 /64，因为主机的临时 IPv6 地址会在其 /64 "
"之内变化。注册指通过邮箱、手机号或单点登录完成的自助注册；管理员创建的账户不算。登录只计成功的登录。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:32
msgid ""
"Email addresses reach one mailbox when they match after dropping "
"everything from a `+` in the part before the `@`, for every provider, and"
" for Gmail also the dots there (`googlemail.com` counts as `gmail.com`). "
"So `jane.doe+test@example.com` and `jane.doe@example.com` match, and at "
"Gmail `jane.doe` and `janedoe` are one mailbox too."
msgstr ""
"两个邮箱地址在去掉从 `+` 起到 `@` 之前的内容后相同，就视为指向同一个邮箱，这适用于所有邮箱服务商；对 "
"Gmail，还会去掉这部分中的点号（`googlemail.com` 视同 `gmail.com`）。因此 "
"`jane.doe+test@example.com` 与 `jane.doe@example.com` 相匹配；在 "
"Gmail，`jane.doe` 与 `janedoe` 也是同一个邮箱。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:34
msgid ""
"`activity_profile` and `same_client` are compared only between accounts "
"that some other evidence already links, so behaviour alone never links "
"two accounts. They only strengthen a link found another way."
msgstr ""
"`activity_profile` 和 `same_client` "
"只在已被其他依据关联的账户之间比较，因此仅凭行为永远不会关联两个账户。它们只会加强通过其他方式发现的关联。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:36
msgid "From links to groups"
msgstr "从关联到分组"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:38
msgid ""
"Each kind of evidence counts once per pair, however many addresses carry "
"it: sharing six addresses of one provider's pool is one fact about the "
"pair, not six. Two accounts join one group when the evidence between that"
" pair reaches 5. Every kind drawn on an address weighs less than that, so"
" no single kind of address evidence links two accounts. Two kinds do, "
"even on one address: registering close together, being active in the same"
" hours, or both signing in and sending requests from it. Two people "
"behind one home or office router who both sign in and use the API, or use"
" it in the same hours, therefore form a group, at the lowest score. A "
"group with no evidence but shared addresses is marked **Shared addresses "
"only** in the console and `address_only` in the API. Using an address in "
"the same hours counts as sharing it; registering from it close together "
"does not, and neither does identity or behaviour evidence."
msgstr ""
"每种依据对一对账户只计一次，不论它出现在多少个地址上：共用同一运营商地址池中的六个地址，对这对账户来说是一个事实，而不是六个。两个账户之间的依据权重之和达到"
" 5 时，它们归入同一个分组。基于地址的每种依据权重都低于 "
"5，所以任何单独一种地址依据都不会关联两个账户。两种依据就会，哪怕在同一个地址上：注册时间相近、在相同时段活跃，或者都从这个地址登录并发送请求。因此，同一个家庭或办公室路由器后面的两个人，如果都登录并使用"
" API，或者在相同时段使用 API，就会以最低得分组成一个分组。如果一个分组除了共用地址之外没有任何依据，控制台会把它标注为 **Shared "
"addresses only**，API 中则为 "
"`address_only`。在相同时段使用同一地址也算作共用地址；从同一地址相近时间注册则不算，身份或行为方面的依据也不算。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:40
msgid ""
"Because each merge needs strong evidence between a pair, a chain of weak "
"links cannot pull strangers into one group. A group's score is the sum of"
" the weights of every linked pair in it, so larger and more tightly "
"linked groups score higher. The score and **Why these accounts** cover "
"every linked pair in the group, including pairs too weak to have merged "
"on their own."
msgstr ""
"由于每次合并都要求一对账户之间有足够强的依据，一串弱关联无法把互不相识的人拉进同一个分组。分组的得分是其中每一对关联账户的权重之和，因此更大、关联更紧密的分组得分更高。得分和"
" **Why these accounts** 涵盖分组内每一对有关联的账户，包括那些依据不足以单独合并的账户对。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:42
msgid ""
"A group of more than 10 accounts is usually a shared network rather than "
"one person. The scan raises the bar inside such a group until its parts "
"are plausible and reports the parts that remain. Whatever stays that "
"large is listed apart, under the components linked too loosely to be one "
"person's, so that the limit is visible rather than silent. A group that "
"same-mailbox or same-browser evidence holds together is reported whole, "
"however large: that is one person with many accounts."
msgstr ""
"超过 10 "
"个账户的分组通常是一个共享网络，而不是一个人。扫描会在这样的分组内部逐步提高门槛，直到各部分都合理，再报告剩下的部分。仍然这么大的部分会单独列出，归入关联过于松散、不像一个人所有的组件，这样上限的作用是可见的，而不是悄无声息。由同一邮箱或同一浏览器依据维系的分组则不论多大都会完整报告：那是一个人拥有许多账户。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:44
msgid "Shared networks and the operator's own accounts"
msgstr "共享网络与运营方自己的账户"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:46
msgid ""
"An office, a campus, a VPN exit or a mobile carrier puts unrelated people"
" on one address. An address that more than 5 accounts used in the window "
"links nobody, and the result says how many addresses it set aside. A "
"browser holding more than 10 accounts is treated as a shared computer in "
"the same way."
msgstr ""
"办公室、校园网、VPN 出口或移动运营商会让互不相关的人共用一个地址。窗口内被超过 5 "
"个账户使用过的地址不会关联任何人，结果中会说明有多少个地址因此被搁置。同样，登录了超过 10 个账户的浏览器被视为共用电脑。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:48
msgid ""
"Administrator, internal and service accounts are never linked: they share"
" the operator's own addresses by design. They still count towards an "
"address's 5 accounts, so an address the operator's staff use is treated "
"as shared."
msgstr ""
"管理员、内部账户和服务账户永远不会被关联：它们本来就共用运营方自己的地址。但它们仍计入一个地址的 5 "
"个账户上限，因此运营方员工使用的地址会被视为共享地址。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:50
msgid ""
"Requests that the gateway or another service sends on an account's behalf"
" say nothing about where the person is, so the scan skips them: batch "
"work, cloud-agent sandboxes and synthetic probes. An address the gateway "
"could not attribute to a client (see [Trusted Proxies and Client IPs"
"](trusted-proxies-and-client-ips.md)) is ignored. Private addresses "
"count, because the gateway records one only for a network authorized as "
"direct clients."
msgstr ""
"网关或其他服务代表账户发送的请求说明不了这个人在哪里，所以扫描会跳过它们：批处理任务、云端 agent "
"沙箱和合成探测请求。网关无法归属到某个客户端的地址（见[可信代理与客户端 IP](trusted-proxies-and-client-"
"ips.md)）会被忽略。私有地址会被计入，因为网关只会为被授权为直连客户端的网络记录私有地址。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:52
msgid "The window"
msgstr "时间窗口"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:54
msgid ""
"Registrations, sign-ins and requests count only inside the window. A "
"browser or a mailbox is not bound to it, but links accounts only when one"
" of them was active in it; a dormant account that shares a mailbox with "
"an active one is still reported. Accounts stay signed in to a browser "
"until they sign out of it, so `same_browser` reflects the browsers that "
"hold the accounts now."
msgstr ""
"注册、登录和请求只计入窗口之内的。浏览器和邮箱不受窗口限制，但只有当其中一个账户在窗口内活跃过时才会关联账户；与活跃账户共用邮箱的休眠账户仍会被报告。账户在浏览器中保持登录，直到从该浏览器退出，因此"
" `same_browser` 反映的是目前登录着这些账户的浏览器。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:56
msgid "Caveats"
msgstr "注意事项"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:58
msgid ""
"A household, a lab or a small office shares an address, and its members "
"may sign up on the same day. Read the evidence before acting on a group."
msgstr "一个家庭、一个实验室或一个小办公室会共用一个地址，其成员也可能在同一天注册。对某个分组采取行动之前，先读一读它的依据。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:59
msgid ""
"The console lets one person sign in to several accounts on purpose. "
"`same_browser` shows that one browser holds the accounts, not that the "
"deployment's rules were broken."
msgstr "控制台有意允许一个人登录多个账户。`same_browser` 表明这些账户登录在同一个浏览器中，并不表明违反了部署的规则。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:60
msgid ""
"The scan reads where and when accounts registered, signed in and sent "
"requests. A deployment that runs it should say so in its privacy policy, "
"and should use it as input to a person's decision, not as grounds for "
"automated enforcement."
msgstr "扫描会读取账户在何时、何地注册、登录和发送请求。运行它的部署应在自己的隐私政策中说明，并且应把结果作为人工决策的参考，而不是自动处罚的依据。"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:62
msgid "Admin API"
msgstr "管理 API"

#: ../developer/duplicate-accounts.md:64
msgid ""
"`GET /admin/users/duplicate-accounts` needs admin authentication (a "
"console session or `ADMIN_TOKEN`)."
msgstr "`GET /admin/users/duplicate-accounts` 需要管理员认证（控制台会话或 `ADMIN_TOKEN`）。"

